29,2,,status,Yumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Oh no! Setting up every morning takes way too long, and those unplanned shuffles sound like a total nightmare for our schedule!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"We are paying for the area regardless of headcount, but every single move costs us money per desk. Frequent changes are inefficient.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It's worse than I thought. The current plan creates ""winners"" and ""losers"" regarding sunlight, and arrival times make ""first-come"" unfair.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The noise levels are inconsistent, and the physical setup of the desks takes days to perfect. Constant moving would be a disaster for comfort.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Yumi,,I found out that sitting near each other really helps us work! New people learn faster and we communicate way better.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Toshio, if moving costs money and takes time, maybe we should just pick one spot and stay there?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Toshio,,That would be the most cost-effective approach. Frequent shuffling is a waste of the budget.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"But if we just ""stay there,"" the people stuck against the wall will be unhappy. We need a system that is fair.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,Fairness is irrelevant if the desk is noisy or the chair is wrong. We need stability to maintain a functional workstation.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"But we can't forget the teamwork! If we are too separated or just random, we lose that magic of overhearing helpful things.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Rin,,I just don't want to spend ten minutes every morning plugging in cables. That's forever when you're busy!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, if we choose a fixed layout, we avoid the recurring facilities charges. That solves the budget concern.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Fixed desks are stable, but we must decide how to assign them so it isn't just based on who got here first.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,Exactly. A fixed assignment allows us to optimize for sound and ergonomics without daily frustration.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"If we do fixed desks, can we group people by how they work so we still talk to each other?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Rin,,That sounds like a great plan! Let's make sure we don't have to move our boxes every few weeks.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I agree. Stability is the only logical choice given the billing and the installation costs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I can support fixed desks, provided the assignment process is transparent and considers the window access.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shion,,I'm satisfied. Stability ensures the physical environment remains tolerable.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"I'm on board! As long as we are grouped to keep the communication flowing, fixed is fine.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
