55,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A sounds like a morning nightmare and Option B sounds like those messy shuffles. I vote C!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A and B both incur unnecessary costs and time losses. Option C is the only fiscally responsible choice.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Option A is unfair due to arrival times. Option B is just delaying the inevitable. I vote for C.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A and B are logically unsound for ergonomics and noise management. I vote for C.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option C lets us group by function, which means we'll keep talking and learning from each other. I vote C!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Rin,,Everyone seems to agree! This was easier than I thought!,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It is the only conclusion that satisfies the constraints of the budget and the facilities.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,We will just need to be very careful about who gets the window seats in Option C.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Shion,,"As long as the noise is managed, I have no further objections.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Yumi,,Yay! We get to stay together and keep the team spirit high!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
